Session 3 summary — stopping at the relay boundary with the fix built and ready to validate.

**Where the criteria stand:** 1/2/4/8/16-node CAW multipath are 100% complete in criteria.json. At 32 nodes, 19 of 20 tests PASS; the sole remaining blocker is `cache_coherency@32/caw` (FAIL from yesterday's ladder: test1 saw one ghost dirent after the unlink storm).

**What this session established:**

1. **Proven on-disk double-allocation** (static, third-party-verifiable): after the failed ladder run, `unlink_visibility`'s dir fork and `.posix_multi`'s fork both referenced the same physical blocks (fsb 1311015, 1835313) — all six of uv-dir's blocks were re-handed out by the allocator across six different AGs. Every existing fence-violation probe (PROBE-A, P125, P88, P75, P79, P121, P117, P70/74) was silent on the 24 nodes with surviving journals. A GPT consult (RULE 5) ranked "false-fresh acquire discarding CIL-resident allocation state" as the top mechanism; I built the lineage-certificate probe (P130) and discard-lifecycle probe (P131) to catch it — both stayed silent in the live repro, so that mechanism is refuted and the double-alloc root remains open, now with much tighter instrumentation.

2. **Root-caused and fixed a second, catastrophic bug caught live by the new repro harness** (`scripts/dblalloc_repro.sh`): peers looking up freshly-created files read the inode cluster's disk location before the carver's chunk-init ever destaged — the block still held a prior owner's urandom data, the read verifier hard-failed with no retry path, and posix_multi collapsed 0/32. Cluster-init durability was tied only to AG-DLM release while name visibility travels via dir-DLM. Fix: synchronous write of the fully-CRC'd cluster buffer at carve time (`P133-ICLUSTER-SYNCINIT`, once per 64 inodes) — build 0.10.110 / srcversion 76FA993D is compiled but **not yet deployed**.

3. **Tooling that persists** (RULE 3): the one-command repro harness, `scripts/xref_owners.py` (quiesced-image dual-ownership fsck — this is what proved both the corruption and, later, iter_1b's cleanliness), and per-iteration journal capture that beats the fast journald rotation on nodes 1-8.

**Next session:** run repro iterations on build 76FA993D (expect the posix_multi collapse gone), watch for uv-ghost/double-alloc recurrence with the xref checker, then re-run the full 32/caw ladder to flip cache_coherency to PASS, regression-check 16/8/4/2/1, and only then write the criteria marker. Full playbook is in memory `AAA-ccloop8ba7-sess3-END-state-and-next-steps`.

